{
  "_about": "How each prose surface treats each writing tell. Tell ids come from ~/.claude/assets/reports/20261027-prose-capability-scour/p0-tells.md; the patterns themselves live in style/thesaurus.jsonl and scripts/style/prose-lint.py. Owner rulings 2026-10-27 (decision page prose-consolidation-p1): D1a this file, D2a verdict opener blocks in files and commits and advises in chat, D3a sentence caps, D4a zero em-dash budget everywhere, D5c doc-writing.md governs every human-facing doc. A tell no ruling covers records today's behaviour unchanged.",
  "actions": {
    "block": "the gate refuses the reply, write or commit",
    "block-pair": "counts toward a block when two or more block-pair tells appear together (chat only)",
    "warn": "a note to the agent; nothing is refused",
    "score": "adds its weight to the prose-lint score; a score above lint_score_block blocks",
    "off": "not checked on this surface"
  },
  "surfaces": {
    "chat": "the agent's final reply (format-gate-stop.sh)",
    "doc": "markdown, html and txt written by Edit or Write (guard-prose-quality.sh, doc-voice-gate.py)",
